{
  "year": 2021,
  "pointsSystem": "Official CrossFit Games scaled points table (reintroduced 2019). Each event is worth 100 points to the winner; remaining places descend on a table whose step size scales to the number of athletes still competing. With the full field (Events 1-9) points fall by 3 per place from the top (100, 97, 94, 91, 88, 85, 82, 79, 76, 73, 70, ...). After the cut to 30 (Event 10) the spread widens (100, 96, 92, 88, 84, 80, ...), and after the cut to 20 (Events 11-15) points fall by 5 per place (100, 95, 90, 85, 80, 75, ...). Tied athletes share the higher place and its points. Final standing is the sum of event points (higher = better).",
